<Base title="Research — Sekiya" description="Sekiya's four agent-behavior research programmes and preserved Research Record.">
  <header class="page-head shell"><p class="kicker">Research</p><h1>Autonomous agents, studied as behavioral entities.</h1><p class="page-sub">Four programmes organize behavior under controlled variation. None has yet established agent-behavior findings or selected its first experiment.</p></header>
  <section class="section shell"><div class="institute-grid"><div><h3>What is established</h3><p>Research has four programmes: Agent Behaviour &amp; Emergence, Agentic Systems &amp; Engineering, Evaluation &amp; Measurement, and Multi-Agent &amp; Human-Agent Systems.</p></div><div><h3>What is required</h3><p>Bounded, reproducible claims; discriminating interventions; and replication where the claim requires it.</p></div><div><h3>What remains open</h3><p>Measurements, experiment families, the first study and any question-derived apparatus remain undecided. The programmes do not activate them.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="ruled-section shell" aria-label="Research Record"><ResearchIndex /></section>
</Base>
